;; The import system (PY5e; PYI-SPEC.md §9's single-file imports): import-name, import-from and
;; import-star, and builtins.__import__, after importlib._bootstrap's __import__, _gcd_import,
;; _find_and_load and _handle_fromlist. A module is found on sys.path (a package's submodules on its
;; __path__): DIR/NAME/__init__.py (a package), DIR/NAME.py, else DIR/NAME as a namespace package; its
;; source is compiled to the IR by the host (SetCompiler: the reader and arbace.python.compile) and run
;; as the module's body. The built-in modules are builtins and sys; the C modules of CPython are PY6's
;; Go ports (survey §6.6), so their import is a ModuleNotFoundError until then. importlib._bootstrap as
;; the import system itself (PYS12) is PY6's: no finders, loaders or specs yet (__spec__ is None).


